      "content": "The idea of wanting the 'stain' gone is a profound expression of wanting the pain to stop. It is exhausting to constantly try to patch something that feels fundamentally flawed. Instead of trying to erase yourself, perhaps you could explore what it would feel like to let go of the pressure to be perfect for them. Sometimes the greatest strength is found not in fixing the cracks, but in accepting where they are.",
      "source": "target",
